      "id": 1,
      "text": "Sherrills Ford got its name from the ford Adam Sherrill crossed in 1747, marking the first European settlement west of the Catawba River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Sherrills_Ford,_North_Carolina",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Neill–Turner–Lester House and the Miles Alexander Sherrill House in Sherrills Ford are listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sherrills_Ford%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Mountain Creek Park spans 606 acres, offering biking, hiking, and trail‑running trails that wind through Sherrills Ford’s wooded hills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sherrills_Ford%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A satellite office of the Catawba County Sheriff’s Department sits in Sherrills Ford, alongside the community library that preserves local history.",
